---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const title = "About - Average Time Calculator";
const description =
  "About the Average Time Calculator — an independent, free utility for averaging time durations and clock times. No ads, no accounts, no data upload.";
const dateModified = "2026-09-03";
const datePublished = "2026-08-13";

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "Organization",
      "@id": "https://www.average-time-calculator.com/#organization",
      name: "Average Time Calculator",
      url: "https://www.average-time-calculator.com/",
      sameAs: ["https://github.com/jiusongvip/average-time-calculator"],
      foundingDate: "2026-08-13",
    },
    {
      "@type": "AboutPage",
      "@id": "https://www.average-time-calculator.com/about/#webpage",
      url: "https://www.average-time-calculator.com/about/",
      name: "About - Average Time Calculator",
      description,
      inLanguage: "en",
      datePublished,
      dateModified,
      publisher: {
        "@id": "https://www.average-time-calculator.com/#organization",
      },
      mainEntity: {
        "@id": "https://www.average-time-calculator.com/about/#article",
      },
    },
    {
      "@type": "WebSite",
      "@id": "https://www.average-time-calculator.com/#website",
      url: "https://www.average-time-calculator.com/",
      name: "Average Time Calculator",
      description,
      inLanguage: "en",
      publisher: {
        "@id": "https://www.average-time-calculator.com/#organization",
      },
    },
    {
      "@type": "TechArticle",
      "@id": "https://www.average-time-calculator.com/about/#article",
      headline: "About this calculator",
      description,
      inLanguage: "en",
      datePublished,
      dateModified,
      author: {
        "@id": "https://www.average-time-calculator.com/#organization",
      },
      publisher: {
        "@id": "https://www.average-time-calculator.com/#organization",
      },
      mainEntityOfPage: {
        "@id": "https://www.average-time-calculator.com/about/#webpage",
      },
    },
  ],
};
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} canonical="https://www.average-time-calculator.com/about/" schema={schema}>
  <section class="section-pad">
    <div class="page-shell max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-emerald-700">About</p>
      <h1 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-[-0.04em] text-zinc-950 sm:text-4xl">About this calculator</h1>
      <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-zinc-600">
        Average Time Calculator is an independent utility for people who work with time data. It is built to be faster than a spreadsheet and clearer than a single average, with no accounts, ads, or server-side data collection.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm font-medium text-zinc-500">Built and maintained by the Average Time Calculator team</p>

      <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-zinc-950">What does this calculator do?</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-600">
        This calculator finds the mean of a set of durations or clock times. For durations, each value is converted to seconds, summed, and divided by the count. For clock times, the page uses circular averaging so values such as 23:50 and 00:10 average close to 00:00 instead of 12:00.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-zinc-950">How are the calculations verified?</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-600">
        Every formula maps to a standard spreadsheet function or published definition. For example, Google's documentation defines the AVERAGE function as one that "returns the numerical average value in a dataset" (<a href="https://support.google.com/docs/answer/3093615" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="font-medium text-emerald-700 hover:underline">Google Support</a>), which is the arithmetic this tool applies to durations. Clock time mode follows the definition of a circular mean from <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Circular_mean" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="font-medium text-emerald-700 hover:underline">Wikipedia</a>.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-4 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-zinc-200 bg-zinc-50 p-6">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-zinc-950">Free and private</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-600">No account, no sign-up, and no time data is uploaded or stored on a server.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-zinc-200 bg-zinc-50 p-6">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-zinc-950">Built for real data</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-600">Mixed formats, weighted records, CSV import, and shareable result links are supported.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-zinc-200 bg-zinc-50 p-6">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-zinc-950">Editorial standards</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-600">Every formula is checked against public references and spreadsheet functions. Errors reported by users are corrected and logged publicly.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-zinc-200 bg-zinc-50 p-6">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-zinc-950">Public and auditable</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-600">Every calculation is documented and mapped to standard spreadsheet functions, so anyone can review the parser, the circular-mean math, and every calculation.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-zinc-950">How can I contact the team?</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-600">
        Open a GitHub issue to report bugs, request features, or ask about the math. The source code is also on GitHub for anyone to review.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <a href="https://github.com/jiusongvip/average-time-calculator/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="rounded-lg border border-zinc-200 bg-zinc-50 p-6 transition hover:border-emerald-300 hover:bg-emerald-50/60">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-zinc-950">GitHub issues</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-600">Report bugs, request features, or ask how the math works. Issues are public so anyone can see the answer.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="https://github.com/jiusongvip/average-time-calculator" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="rounded-lg border border-zinc-200 bg-zinc-50 p-6 transition hover:border-emerald-300 hover:bg-emerald-50/60">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-zinc-950">Source code</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-600">Read the parser, circular-mean math, and every formula used on this page.</p>
        </a>
      </div>

      <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-zinc-950">When was this page last updated?</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-600">Each update is recorded here so visitors can see the page is actively maintained and reviewed.</p>
      <ul class="mt-6 space-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-600">
        <li class="flex flex-col gap-1 sm:flex-row sm:gap-4">
          <time class="shrink-0 font-mono text-xs font-semibold text-emerald-700">2026-09-03</time>
          <span>Added sameAs entity links to schema, strengthened references section with authoritative citations, and added Contact and Terms of use sections.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex flex-col gap-1 sm:flex-row sm:gap-4">
          <time class="shrink-0 font-mono text-xs font-semibold text-emerald-700">2026-08-17</time>
          <span>Added a verification guide, standard deviation and per-value deviation, day-unit input, open-source links, and three new FAQ entries.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex flex-col gap-1 sm:flex-row sm:gap-4">
          <time class="shrink-0 font-mono text-xs font-semibold text-emerald-700">2026-08-13</time>
          <span>Initial public release with duration and clock time modes, weighted and running averages, CSV import and export, and shareable result links.</span>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>